

# The BUILT SITE. Generated by generate_site.py on every run and published
# to Pages from an uploaded artifact, so it never needs to be in git.
#
# It was committed until the repo reached 157MB of pack -- a 4MB
# index.html rewritten every 5 minutes, each version storing nearly in
# full because the odds data throughout it changes. Pages clones the repo
# to build, so deployments got slower until they stopped finishing.
#
# Untracked here, still written to disk, still uploaded as the artifact.
docs/index.html
docs/movements/

# ...but the BRAND ASSETS stay tracked. They are generated ONCE by
# scripts/generate_brand_assets.py, not on every build, and that script needs
# Pillow -- which the workflow doesn't install and this machine doesn't have.
#
# Ignoring all of docs/ removed the only copy of them: the runner rebuilt
# index.html and movements/ from source, uploaded an artifact with no launch
# images in it, and iOS -- finding no matching size -- fell back to the white
# screen the whole feature exists to replace.
#
# They cost ~200KB total and change perhaps twice a year, so committing them
# has none of the problems that made the 4MB-per-run index.html untenable.
!docs/splash-*.png
!docs/favicon*
!docs/icon-*.png
!docs/apple-touch-icon.png
!docs/og-share-card.png
!docs/manifest.json
!docs/.nojekyll
# ESPN RESPONSE CACHE. scripts/backfill_espn_fight_stats.py caches every HTTP
# response here keyed by URL hash, which is what makes a re-run cheap.
#
# It must never be committed. The workflow's commit step is `git add -A --
# data/ docs/`, so the moment that script started running in CI the cache
# began landing in the repo -- and a fresh shallow checkout starts with an
# empty one, so each run would add whatever it fetched, forever. A local
# working copy of this directory is 453MB across 45,000 files.
#
# That is the same failure that already happened once with the built site:
# the pack reached 157MB, Pages clones the repo to build, and deployments
# got slower until they stopped finishing. Ignoring it costs nothing --
# it is a cache, it regenerates on demand, and CI's checkout is fresh
# every run so it was never getting a cache hit from git anyway.
data/.espn_cache/

__pycache__/
.DS_Store

# Free-tier payload and its redaction manifest, rebuilt every run.
build/

# Generated by generate_site.py on every run, like docs/index.html.
# Committing it meant a permanently dirty tree and a rebase that refused.
docs/welcome.html

# Local wrangler state (build cache, dev bindings).
.wrangler/

# Legal pages, rebuilt every run alongside welcome.html.
docs/terms.html
docs/privacy.html
docs/refunds.html
